## Section 4: Experience (Timeline)

### Current Issues
- The entire section is **grey-on-grey** — incredibly hard to read
- Job title and company name blend into the background
- Date badges are dark-on-dark (illegible)
- Tech tags are flat grey pills with no personality
- Timeline line is jarringly bright neon blue vs the muted cards
- Excessive dead space above the first card

### Redesign Steps

1. **Contrast overhaul** — `.timeline-role`: `color: #ffffff; font-weight: 700; font-size: 1.15rem`. `.timeline-company`: `color: var(--accent-blue-light) (#5ac8fa); font-weight: 600`. `.timeline-desc` (body text): `color: rgba(255,255,255,0.8)`
2. **Date badge redesign** — `background: rgba(0,122,255,0.2); color: #5ac8fa; font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.75rem; font-weight: 600; padding: 4px 12px; border-radius: 6px; letter-spacing: 0.05em`
3. **Tech tag upgrade** — `background: rgba(0,122,255,0.1); color: rgba(255,255,255,0.9); border: 0.5px solid rgba(0,122,255,0.3); border-radius: 6px; font-size: 0.7rem; padding: 4px 10px`
4. **Harmonize timeline line** — Reduce line opacity: `border-left: 2px solid rgba(0,122,255,0.4)`. Dot glow: `box-shadow: 0 0 6px rgba(0,122,255,0.5)` (softer)
5. **Reduce dead space** — Section title `margin-bottom: 24px`, gap between items: `16px`
6. **Entry animation** — Each `.timeline-item` fades in from the left with `transform: translateX(-20px); opacity: 0` → `translateX(0); opacity: 1` on scroll

