## Cross-Cutting Improvements

### A. Section Dividers
Add between every section: `<hr>` styled as `height: 0.5px; background: linear-gradient(90deg, transparent, rgba(0,122,255,0.3), transparent); border: none; margin: 0 32px`

### B. Scroll Animations
Use `IntersectionObserver` to add `is-visible` class on scroll. Base styles: `opacity: 0; transform: translateY(24px); transition: opacity 0.5s ease, transform 0.5s ease`. Visible: `opacity: 1; transform: translateY(0)`

### C. Global Text Contrast Fix
Inside `@media (max-width: 800px)`:
```css
body { color: rgba(255,255,255,0.92) !important; }
p, .text-body { color: rgba(255,255,255,0.8) !important; }
h1, h2, h3, h4 { color: #ffffff !important; }
```

### D. Card Glass Override Fix
Move the global card styles at L442–464 of [mobile-design.css](file:///Users/vineetkishore/Documents/iCloud%20Drive/Drive%20X/Softwares/Coding%20Projects/Portfolio%20Project/core/css/mobile-design.css) **inside** the `@media (max-width: 800px)` block so they don't bleed to desktop.

### E. Touch Feedback
All interactive elements get: `-webkit-tap-highlight-color: transparent` and on `:active`: `transform: scale(0.97); transition: transform 0.1s ease`

### F. Dynamic Font Sizing
Replace all fixed `px` font sizes with `clamp()`:
- Section titles: `clamp(1.4rem, 5vw, 1.8rem)`
- Body text: `clamp(0.85rem, 2.5vw, 1rem)`
- Badges/tags: `clamp(0.65rem, 2vw, 0.8rem)`

---

## Desktop-Coherence Additions

These four items address elements that **work on desktop but are broken or absent on mobile**, creating a visual disconnect between the two experiences.

### G. Kinetic Text Banner

**Desktop behaviour:** A scrolling marquee of keywords/phrases runs horizontally across the screen between sections, adding dynamism and personality.

**Mobile problem:** The kinetic text is either invisible (hidden by a `display: none` media query) or overflows because font sizes are too large and animation speed is uncalibrated for smaller widths.

**Fix:**
- Re-enable the kinetic text section on mobile (remove any `display: none` override)
- Scale typography: `font-size: clamp(1rem, 4vw, 1.5rem)`
- Reduce animation speed by ~40% (`animation-duration: 25s` instead of `15s`) so it's readable on a narrow viewport
- Ensure `overflow: hidden` on the container to prevent horizontal bleed
- Match the desktop's `color: rgba(255,255,255,0.15)` watermark aesthetic

### H. Project Card Image Proportions

**Desktop behaviour:** Each project card has a visual area (emoji/image) that occupies a proportional top section, with content below — the card feels balanced.

**Mobile problem:** The visual area either stretches to fill the entire screen height (making one card = 2 full scroll lengths) or collapses to nothing. The proportions are completely lost.

**Fix:**
- Cap the visual area: `.project-cinema-visual { max-height: 200px; overflow: hidden; border-radius: 16px 16px 0 0 }`
- Constrain emoji icons: render inside a `width: 80px; height: 80px; margin: 0 auto` centered box so they don't float in vast empty space
- The overall card should fit within ~70–80% of the viewport height so the user can always see the card's title and at least the start of the next card (implying there's more content)

### I. Education Achievement Callouts

**Desktop behaviour:** The trophy (🏆) and debate (🎤) achievement lines pop with clear contrast and feel like badges of accomplishment.

**Mobile problem:** Same contrast issue as Experience — the achievement text is dim grey, the emoji icons are tiny, and the entire callout blends into the card background. Users completely miss these.

**Fix:**
- Style achievement items as pills: `display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 6px; background: rgba(0,122,255,0.1); border: 0.5px solid rgba(0,122,255,0.2); border-radius: 8px; padding: 6px 12px; color: rgba(255,255,255,0.9); font-size: 0.8rem`
- Ensure emoji renders at `font-size: 1rem` (not inherited tiny size)
- Add `margin: 4px` between achievement pills for clean wrapping

### J. Scroll-Triggered Fade-In Parity

**Desktop behaviour:** As the user scrolls, sections and cards fade in with subtle `translateY` + opacity transitions powered by `IntersectionObserver`. This gives the page a living, breathing quality.

**Mobile problem:** Multiple `@media (max-width: 768px)` blocks in [style.css](file:///Users/vineetkishore/Documents/iCloud%20Drive/Drive%20X/Softwares/Coding%20Projects/Portfolio%20Project/core/css/style.css) hardcode `animation: none !important` and `transition: none !important`, killing all scroll-triggered animations. The mobile page feels static and lifeless compared to desktop.

**Fix:**
- **Do NOT globally disable animations on mobile.** Instead, audit each `animation: none` override in [style.css](file:///Users/vineetkishore/Documents/iCloud%20Drive/Drive%20X/Softwares/Coding%20Projects/Portfolio%20Project/core/css/style.css) and remove only the ones that kill scroll-triggered entry animations (keep any that disable CPU-heavy particle effects or complex 3D transforms)
- Re-enable `IntersectionObserver`-based `.is-visible` class toggling on mobile (gate by `window.innerWidth <= 800` in [app.js](file:///Users/vineetkishore/Documents/iCloud%20Drive/Drive%20X/Softwares/Coding%20Projects/Portfolio%20Project/core/js/app.js))
- Use lightweight transitions only: `opacity 0.5s ease, transform 0.5s ease` — no heavy `clip-path` or `filter` animations that would hurt mobile performance
- Apply to: `.about-card`, `.timeline-item`, `.project-cinema-card`, `.skill-group`, `.education-card`, `.insight-card`

